  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A photoelectron is emitted when a photon of energy <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E\"></span> is incident on a metal surface.</p>\n<p>The work function of the surface is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Φ\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the maximum possible speed of the photoelectron as it leaves the surface?<br/><br/></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{\\frac{2E-Φ}{m_{e}}}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{\\frac{E-Φ}{m_{e}}}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{\\frac{E-Φ}{m_{e}h}}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{\\frac{2E-Φ}{m_{e}h}}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
